      "Language": "eng",
      "Abstract": {"AbstractText": "We report on an unusual patient with a threatened occlusive dissection, in whom prolonged (48-hr) inflation of a balloon catheter with localized heparin infusion proved successful. This intracoronary infusion catheter maintained distal coronary flow on a unique spiral coil design, and may provide an alternative or a bridge to emergency operation or stent implantation."},
